==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|prōsecūtus}}, perfect participle of {{m|la|prōsequor}}. Compare {{m|en|persecute}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|prosecut}}

# {{label|en|transitive|legal}} To [[start]] [[criminal]] [[proceeding]]s against.
#: ''to '''prosecute''' a man for trespass, or for a riot''
#* Milton
#*: To acquit themselves and '''prosecute''' their foes.
# {{label|en|transitive|legal}} To [[charge]], [[try]].
# To seek to obtain by legal process.
#: ''to '''prosecute''' a right or a claim in a court of law''
# {{label|en|transitive}} To [[pursue]] something to the [[end]].
#: ''to '''prosecute''' a scheme, hope, or claim''
#* Shakespeare
#*: I am beloved of beauteous Hermia; / Why should not I, then, '''prosecute''' my right?

